I see a small vegetable shop.
I stand in front of that shop.
A man is standing in the shop.
"Hello," I say to him.
"Hello," he says to me.
"Do you have fresh tomatoes?" I ask.
"Yes, there are good tomatoes," he says.
"I need tomatoes and onions," I say.
He takes some tomatoes and onions.
He weighs it.
"How much is the price?" I ask.
"Eighty rupees," he says.
I take money from my bag.
I give him eighty rupees.
He gives me the vegetables.
I carefully put those vegetables into my bag.
I walk towards home.
